          "kind": "issue",
          "number": "47",
          "externalId": "iss_034WGCE66WJmQ6lSSwXkoh"
        },
        "kind": "issue",
        "title": "Webhooks for push, tag and pull request events",
        "body": "We'd like to run CI (Woodpecker) and automatic deploys from Pushin repositories. Both learn about changes from forge webhooks, so without them a push or a tag builds nothing.\n\nWhat we need:\n - Per-repository webhooks, configurable in the UI and the API.\n - Events: push (with branch and before/after SHA), tag created, and pull request opened, updated or closed.\n - Payloads in the GitHub or Gitea shape, since the API already follows GitHub.\n - A signature header (HMAC-SHA256 with a shared secret).\n - A delivery log with redelivery, so a missed delivery can be seen and fixed.\n\nThanks for the nice product!",
        "state": "open",
        "stateRaw": "open",
        "isDraft": false,
        "author": {
          "forge": "pushin",
          "instance": "pushin.eu",
          "login": "antoine",
          "id": "462",
          "avatarUrl": "https://cdn.pushin.eu/-/avatars/u_034NWUr8cxFmBRn6njSdYT",
          "url": "https://pushin.eu/antoine",
          "typeRaw": "User",
          "isBotHint": false
        },
